{title: Unclean Unclean}
{subtitle: Leviticus 13:1–46}
{key: Bbm}
{tempo: 75}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bbm] | [Bbm] | [Bbm] | [Bbm] |
| [Bbm] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
The LORD spoke to Moses and Aaron
Bring the swelling, rash, or bright spot to the priest
The hair has turned white, the sore is deep
He examines the [Gb]skin, de[Ab]clares him un[Bbm]clean
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
If it looks shallow, the hair is not white
Isolate [Gb]the person [Ab]for seven [Bbm]days
Check again on the seventh day
If it has [Gb]faded, [Ab]he is clean [Bbm]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Wear torn clothes, let the hair hang down
Cover the up[Gb]per lip, [Ab]stand a[Bbm]lone
Cry out loud, "Unclean! Unclean!"
Live outside the [Gb]camp, in the [Ab]dust and the sun [Bbm]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
If the disease covers head to foot
And it has [Gb]all turned white, [Ab]he is clean [Bbm]
But if raw flesh appears on the skin
The priest [Gb]sees it, de[Ab]clares him un[Bbm]clean
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Wear torn clothes, let the hair hang down
Cover the up[Gb]per lip, [Ab]stand a[Bbm]lone
Cry out loud, "Unclean! Unclean!"
Live outside the [Gb]camp, in the [Ab]dust and the sun
{end_of_chorus}

{comment: Interlude}
| [Bbm] | [Bbm] | [Bbm] | [Gb] [Ab] | ×2
| [Bbm] |

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
A boil or a burn, a spot in the [Gb]flesh
The priest ex[Ab]amines, waits for [Bbm]the sign
If it spreads, it is a defiling disease
If [Gb]it [Ab]fades, he is clean
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
Unclean! Unclean!
Live alone out[Gb]side the camp
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Outro (instrumental)}
